# Repository line-ending policy: LF everywhere, Windows checkouts included.
# core.autocrlf does not get a vote.
#
# Why it matters here beyond tidiness: a CR that reaches a shell script or a
# sourced env file produces failures that look like anything but line endings —
# `$'\r': command not found`, or a value that silently carries a trailing
# carriage return into whatever consumes it.
#
# Applied GOING FORWARD: files normalise as they are touched, so adding this does
# not rewrite the whole tree in one diff. To convert the rest deliberately:
#   git add --renormalize . && git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings to LF"
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts are the exception — cmd.exe requires CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never let git rewrite the bytes of a binary asset.
*.pfx    binary
*.p12    binary
*.jks    binary
*.ks     binary
*.keystore binary
*.tar    binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.tgz    binary
*.zip    binary
*.jar    binary
*.war    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.docx   binary
